{
  "message": "I reviewed the rewards activity for both verified card accounts. The transaction records do not show a missing reward on the 23 completed purchases reviewed.",
  "results": {
    "Gold Rewards Card": {
      "transactions_reviewed": 12,
      "rewards_from_reviewed_transactions": "5,305 points",
      "cash_back_equivalent": "$53.05",
      "account_reward_balance": "7,021 points ($70.21)",
      "difference": "1,716 points ($17.16) more than the reviewed transactions"
    },
    "EcoCard": {
      "transactions_reviewed": 11,
      "rewards_from_reviewed_transactions": "4,839 points",
      "account_reward_balance": "4,839 points ($48.39)",
      "difference": "None"
    }
  },
  "interpretation": [
    "The EcoCard total reconciles exactly with the reward balance shown.",
    "The Gold Rewards Card has 1,716 points beyond the transactions reviewed, which likely reflects rewards earned before the activity available in this transaction history or another account-level rewards entry. The records I can access do not identify the source of that difference.",
    "Although the transaction system labels rewards as points, Gold Rewards Card points represent cash back at 1 point = $0.01 when redeemed as a statement or checking-account credit. EcoCard rewards are sustainability points and also redeem at $0.01 per point for those options.",
    "Rewards are rounded down to whole points, so fractional points are not included."
  ],
  "next_step": "If your statement shows a lower total than these balances, the discrepancy may involve a redemption, adjustment, or statement-period cutoff that is not included in the transaction history. I can help investigate further if you provide the statement period or the total shown on each statement."
}
